# AscThem Medication Intelligence Agent Service

This is the first runnable increment of AscThem's medication-intelligence layer. It is a Python FastAPI service containing a LangGraph orchestrator and a mock Pricing, Coupons & Reviews agent. The existing backend/API gateway can call this service after product verification produces a normalized medication context.

## Current workflow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[API request] --> B[Normalize medication]
  B --> C[Route requested agents]
  C -->|pricing| D[Mock pricing agent]
  C -->|future agent| E[Record unavailable]
  D --> F[Build fixed response]
  E --> F
```

Implemented now:

- Deterministic routing for `pricing`, `ddi`, `pharmacovigilance`, and `all`.
- A replaceable `PricingProvider` interface for future authorized GoodRx or SingleCare access.
- Mock pricing, coupon, pharmacy, and review data clearly marked with `isMock: true`.
- A shared source/evidence schema and predefined API response.
- JSONL logs for every run and graph node.
- Optional LangSmith tracing through standard environment variables.
- Explicit `not_implemented` results for DDI and pharmacovigilance instead of fabricated information.

No LLM is used yet. The routing and initial insights are deterministic, which keeps this foundation testable and prevents unsupported medication claims.

## Setup

```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

Run the API:

```powershell
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 3000
```

OpenAPI documentation is available at `http://localhost:3000/docs`.

## Example request

```powershell
$body = @{
  intent = "pricing"
  medication = @{
    ndc = "0002-8215-01"
    drugName = "Example Drug"
    strength = "10 mg"
    dosageForm = "tablet"
    quantity = @{ amount = 30; unit = "tablet" }
  }
  context = @{ postalCode = "10001" }
} | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5

Invoke-RestMethod `
  -Method Post `
  -Uri http://localhost:3000/api/v1/orchestrator/run `
  -ContentType "application/json" `
  -Body $body
```

## Observability

Local logging is always available. Run and node events are appended to `logs/orchestrator.jsonl` unless `ORCHESTRATOR_LOG_PATH` is changed.

To add LangSmith tracing, set:

```text
LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=your-key
LANGSMITH_PROJECT=ascthem-orchestrator
LANGSMITH_HIDE_INPUTS=true
LANGSMITH_HIDE_OUTPUTS=true
```

Keep both hide settings enabled for medication workflows. LangSmith tracing normally captures graph inputs and outputs, which can include medication and user context; these settings retain graph timing and execution visibility while hiding those payloads. Only opaque request/run IDs and routing metadata are deliberately attached as metadata by this service. Do not commit `.env` or API keys.

## Tests

```powershell
pytest
```

## Next increment

Replace `MockPricingProvider` with an authorized provider adapter while preserving the provider contract. Add fixture-based contract tests before returning live commercial pricing to the mobile application.
